---
import Technical from '../Technical.astro';
import data from '../../data/scrolly/recruitment-data.json';
---

<div class="recruitment-notes">
  <Technical title="Validation note — what the checks establish">
    <p>
      The frozen baseline passed 220 tests; six export checks bring the source
      total to 226. Two clean rebuilds checked reproducibility. Twenty
      perturbations examined stability: striker similarity was available in
      202/280 checks and striker ranking in 18/20. These are software and
      analytical checks, not recruitment success rates.
    </p>
    <p>
      CASE-03 is a limited centre-back review with 30 sampled observations and
      unknown continuous viewing duration. Expert/scout and predictive
      validation remain unperformed. Price, contracts, age, injury,
      availability, and context adjustments are outside the baseline.
    </p>
  </Technical>
  <Technical title="Data note — pinned source and verified artifacts">
    <p>
      This story uses the frozen V1 reproduction receipt, profile export,
      similarity query for Katrine Veje, and stored CB defensive-activity
      ranking. All 10 stored nearest-neighbor results were replayed from the
      saved twelve-feature scaler within 1e-10. Every selected candidate’s
      contributions sum to its score within 1e-10.
    </p>
    <p>
      Profile counts and coordinates are real. Opening placement, cluster
      packing, event particles, and architecture positions are explanatory
      layouts. No raw events or complete derived profile tables are served.
    </p>
    <dl>
      <dt>StatsBomb source revision</dt>
      <dd>
        <code>{data.source.revision}</code>
      </dd>
      {Object.entries(data.source.verifiedArtifacts).map(([stage, value]) => (
        <Fragment>
          <dt>{stage} manifest SHA-256</dt>
          <dd>
            <code>{value.manifest}</code>
          </dd>
          {'artifact' in value && (
            <Fragment>
              <dt>{stage} artifact SHA-256</dt>
              <dd>
                <code>{value.artifact}</code>
              </dd>
            </Fragment>
          )}
        </Fragment>
      ))}
    </dl>
  </Technical>
</div>
